  "notes": [
    "NOTES:",
    "• Flat heads on an L3x3x1/4 HDG angle lintel each, 4\" bearing a side (IRC R703.8.3, Table R703.8.3.1). No arch.",
    "• Ties: 2024 IRC Table R703.8.4(1) W2.8, 2 pintle legs, every tie on a stud, extra ties within 12\" of each opening.",
    "• The wythe is dry-bedded on the base flashing: no mortar bond to the beam. The court slides under it.",
    "• Weeps (IRC R703.8.6): open head joints, 3/16\" or more, over the flashing and over each lintel, 33\" o.c. at most.",
    "• Lintel flashing (IRC R703.8.5): the same sheet lapped up the backup and out over the angle, ends turned up 2\" as dams.",
    "• Tie rows are bed joints, 24\" o.c. at most: 16\", 34 2/3\", 48\", 61 1/3\", 85 1/3\" over the base; the door head row is on the cripples.",
    "",
    "KEYED NOTES:",
    "K1  Base bond break and flashing: steel sheet on the beam top under course 1, leg up the backup 2\", drip 3/8\" out."
  ],
